# requirements/data-sources/cross-match.ears
capability: Cross-match
owner: data-sources
requirements:
  - id: DSI-009
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The kernel shall admit a cross-match adapter to a gate only after it agrees with AstropyCrossMatch on the fixture within tolerance."
    rationale: "A remote cross-match must agree with the CPU reference before it is trusted. For CDS X-Match the contract fixture is answered by the live service (Archive live smoke, tools/record_live_data.py) and replayed in CI; this stays draft until those answers are recorded."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: DSI-018
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The system shall cross-match two frames on the local machine with the CPU reference join unless SDP_CROSS_MATCH asks for CDS X-Match."
    rationale: "CDS X-Match has no mirror and was down for days (Leigh's plan execute and record_live_data runs, 2026-10-30), while the work it does (an angular join of two frames SDP already holds) is the CPU reference itself; DSI-009 has not yet admitted X-Match to a gate, so matching here is also the trusted path."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_xmatch_local::test_the_local_join_agrees_with_the_cpu_reference_on_a_crowded_field"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_wiring::test_cross_matching_runs_here_unless_cds_is_asked_for"
  - id: DSI-019
    pattern: event
    text: "When SDP_CROSS_MATCH is auto and CDS X-Match gives no answer or a server error, the system shall cross-match the two frames on the local machine."
    rationale: "Asking CDS first keeps X-Match in use when it is up, while an outage never stops a run; a refusal (a 4xx) is still raised, never papered over."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_xmatch_local::test_when_cds_gives_no_answer_or_a_server_error_the_match_runs_here"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_xmatch_local::test_a_refusal_from_cds_is_raised_and_an_answer_is_used_as_given"
